Package: rbeam
Type: Package
Title: Benchmark Evaluation and Metrics (R Interface)
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Izaskun", "Mallona", email = "izaskun.mallona.work@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2853-7526"))
    )
Description: R interface to the beam Python package. beam stores the scale
    type, polarity, range and allowed transformations of each performance
    metric of a benchmark in a metric card (YAML, JSON Schema), ranks methods
    with multi-criteria aggregations, reports how the ranking changes with
    the weighting, the aggregation and the datasets (SMAA, leave-one-out,
    weight perturbation, rank sensitivity), tests whether methods are
    separable (Friedman, Nemenyi, Skillings-Mack), and fits heterogeneity
    models (mixed-effects variance decomposition, Bradley-Terry trees,
    Plackett-Luce models, network meta-analysis). The R package calls the
    Python package through 'reticulate' and draws the figures with
    'ggplot2'.
URL: https://github.com/imallona/beam
